  "question": {
    "text": "The observed magnetic moment of the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>NCS</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi></math>. The numerical value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>NCS</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> has a magnetic moment of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi></math>. This indicates that the complex has unpaired electrons, which contribute to its magnetic moment.</p><p>Number of unpaired electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math>.<br />So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math>&nbsp;must be in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;oxidation state&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />The numerical value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>, so the complex is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>NCS</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
